CHANGED: In the cleanup phase that flattens the function hierarchy, the evaluator-backed transformations (`reduceConst`, `reduceNonRepPrim`) and the transformations that piggyback on their output now run as a single bottom-up pass per flattening iteration, instead of in every settle round of the inner fixed-point loop. On larger designs we've tested this yielded a ~30% performance bump end-to-end.
